  data: {
    LLM: "Bet the minimum when the target card is high (e.g., a 7). Since you need to beat the card in the SAME SUIT, and 1/4 of your cards are typically the right suit, the odds of having a card higher than a 7 in that specific suit are low. Bet the pool when the target card is a 2 or 3â€”your odds of having *any* higher card of that suit are much better.\n\nPool Management: If the pool is small, bet more aggressively to 'Empty' it and become the next dealer. If the pool is massive, the pressure is on the Banker. As a player, you only risk what you bet, but the Banker is responsible for the pool's health across many rounds. Watch for 'Suit Clustering'â€”if the previous 5 players all lost on a Spade target, the odds of the remaining deck being 'Spade-Rich' are higher.\n\nThe 'Blind' Advantage: While the game is mostly luck, the strategy lies in 'Bet Sizing' relative to the Target Card. A pro player treats Polish Bank like a game of 'Dynamic Odds'. Since you have 3 cards, the probability of hitting a specific suit is ~58%. If the target card is a 4, you have a solid edge against the house. Always bet the maximum allowed when the target is 2, 3, or 4.",
    Player: "Bet the minimum when the target card is high (e.g., a 7). Since you need to beat the card in the SAME SUIT, and 1/4 of your cards are typically the right suit, the odds of having a card higher than a 7 in that specific suit are low. Bet the pool when the target card is a 2 or 3â€”your odds of having *any* higher card of that suit are much better.\n\nPool Management: If the pool is small, bet more aggressively to 'Empty' it and become the next dealer. If the pool is massive, the pressure is on the Banker. As a player, you only risk what you bet, but the Banker is responsible for the pool's health across many rounds. Watch for 'Suit Clustering'â€”if the previous 5 players all lost on a Spade target, the odds of the remaining deck being 'Spade-Rich' are higher.\n\nThe 'Blind' Advantage: While the game is mostly luck, the strategy lies in 'Bet Sizing' relative to the Target Card. A pro player treats Polish Bank like a game of 'Dynamic Odds'. Since you have 3 cards, the probability of hitting a specific suit is ~58%. If the target card is a 4, you have a solid edge against the house. Always bet the maximum allowed when the target is 2, 3, or 4.",
